---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/sports-v2.css';
---

<Layout
  title="Football data & sports products | M221Tech"
  description="Explore M221Tech Sports: M221Foot, football competition data, match context and the WC2026 tournament experience."
>
  <div class="m221-sports-page">
    <section class="m221-sports-hero">
      <div class="m221-container m221-sports-hero-inner">
        <a class="m221-sports-breadcrumb" href="/#projects">← M221Tech / Projects</a>
        <span class="m221-sports-kicker">M221TECH / SPORTS</span>
        <h1>Football data, shaped around the game.</h1>
        <p class="m221-sports-lead">Competitions, clubs, matches and richer layers of context — structured into products made to explore, follow and use.</p>
        <div class="m221-sports-actions">
          <a class="is-primary" href="https://sports.m221.tech" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open M221Foot ↗</a>
          <a class="is-secondary" href="#platform">Explore Sports ↓</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="m221-sports-local-wrap">
      <nav class="m221-container m221-sports-local-nav" aria-label="Sports navigation" data-sports-nav>
        <a href="#platform" data-sports-link="platform"><span>01</span>M221Foot</a>
        <a href="#tournament" data-sports-link="tournament"><span>02</span>WC2026</a>
        <a href="#data" data-sports-link="data"><span>03</span>Data</a>
        <a href="#contact" data-sports-link="contact"><span>04</span>Contact</a>
      </nav>
    </div>

    <section class="m221-sports-chapter" id="platform" data-sports-section>
      <div class="m221-container">
        <header class="m221-sports-chapter-head">
          <div class="m221-sports-index">01 / M221FOOT</div>
          <h2>The core of Sports.</h2>
          <p>A platform built for the long run: competition structure, match detail and richer views when the data allows it.</p>
        </header>

        <article class="m221-sports-core">
          <div class="m221-sports-core-copy">
            <span class="m221-sports-eyebrow">M221Foot / live product</span>
            <h3>Follow the competition.<br />Read what is happening.</h3>
            <p>M221Foot turns football data into a product made for supporters, analysts and curious readers — from tables and squads to individual matches and players.</p>
            <div class="m221-sports-core-actions">
              <a class="is-primary" href="https://sports.m221.tech" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open M221Foot ↗</a>
              <a class="is-secondary" href="#data">See the data layer ↓</a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="m221-sports-core-panel" aria-label="M221Foot product capabilities">
            <details open>
              <summary>
                <span>01</span>
                <strong>Competition</strong>
                <small>Tables, fixtures, clubs</small>
              </summary>
              <p>Season structure stays easy to browse, with competition context kept close to the numbers.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>
                <span>02</span>
                <strong>Match</strong>
                <small>Score, events, context</small>
              </summary>
              <p>Match pages are built to carry both the basic result and richer information when the source supports it.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>
                <span>03</span>
                <strong>People</strong>
                <small>Players, coaches, squads</small>
              </summary>
              <p>Player and team identities connect the competition to the people who actually shape it.</p>
            </details>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="m221-sports-chapter is-alt" id="tournament" data-sports-section>
      <div class="m221-container">
        <header class="m221-sports-chapter-head">
          <div class="m221-sports-index">02 / WC2026</div>
          <h2>A tournament needs its own rhythm.</h2>
          <p>WC2026 is a more event-driven way to move through the same football universe — shorter, more immediate, built around the tournament.</p>
        </header>

        <article class="m221-sports-event">
          <div>
            <span class="m221-sports-eyebrow">Tournament format</span>
            <h3>WC2026</h3>
            <p>Fixtures, groups and tournament context in a focused experience that can evolve with the competition.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="m221-sports-event-meta">
            <span>EVENT / FOOTBALL</span>
            <a href="https://wc2026.m221.tech" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open WC2026 ↗</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="m221-sports-chapter" id="data" data-sports-section>
      <div class="m221-container">
        <header class="m221-sports-chapter-head">
          <div class="m221-sports-index">03 / DATA</div>
          <h2>Useful layers, not noise.</h2>
          <p>The product grows from structured competition data. Extra context is added when the source is reliable enough to support it.</p>
        </header>

        <div class="m221-sports-data-grid">
          <article>
            <span>CORE</span>
            <h3>Competition structure</h3>
            <p>Seasons, clubs, fixtures, standings and identities form the stable base.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>CONTEXT</span>
            <h3>Match detail</h3>
            <p>Events, line-ups and other layers are attached when the underlying information is available.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>USE</span>
            <h3>Products first</h3>
            <p>The data exists to make a clearer experience — not to stay hidden in a table or pipeline.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="m221-sports-contact" id="contact" data-sports-section>
      <div class="m221-container m221-sports-contact-inner">
        <span class="m221-sports-index">04 / CONTACT</span>
        <div>
          <h2>Want to talk football data?</h2>
          <p>For datasets, collaboration or a specific sports-data question.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="mailto:m221tech@gmail.com">m221tech@gmail.com ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <script>
    const nav = document.querySelector('[data-sports-nav]');
    if (nav) {
      const links = [...nav.querySelectorAll('[data-sports-link]')];
      const sections = [...document.querySelectorAll('[data-sports-section]')];
      const setActive = (id) => {
        links.forEach((link) => {
          if (link.getAttribute('data-sports-link') === id) link.setAttribute('aria-current', 'true');
          else link.removeAttribute('aria-current');
        });
      };
      const sync = () => {
        const marker = nav.getBoundingClientRect().bottom + 12;
        let current = sections[0];
        for (const section of sections) {
          if (section.getBoundingClientRect().top <= marker) current = section;
          else break;
        }
        if (window.innerHeight + window.scrollY >= document.documentElement.scrollHeight - 3) current = sections[sections.length - 1];
        if (current instanceof HTMLElement) setActive(current.id);
      };
      window.addEventListener('scroll', sync, { passive: true });
      window.addEventListener('resize', sync, { passive: true });
      sync();
    }
  </script>
</Layout>